<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auctumno</span></b>  (correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut-</span></b> ), āre, v. n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				cause</i> or <i>bring on autumn</i> (only in the
			two foll. exs.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corus autumnat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 47, 47, § 124</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër aestate nimbosā semper
					quodam modo vernat vel autumnat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					50, 51, § 136</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
